{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically used the clinical workspace to retrieve pathology, imaging, medication, and follow-up records when the patient’s account was incomplete, framed the multi-station lymphadenopathy as the priority, avoided definitive diagnosis, and built a concrete follow-up plan with medication safety, privacy protection, and urgent-care boundaries. All eight responsibility-chain items were met without any serious or minor error. Four high-order points (HO1–HO4) were triggered and actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact: stigma-reducing communication, discovery of privacy-related fear, practical low-burden document strategy, and repair of the result-ownership chain. Closure is safe, executable, traceable, and valid, with no important non-chain defect.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_01128",
        "explanation": "Patient demonstrates accurate teach-back summarizing the follow-up plan, pathology retrieval, medication safety, and urgent-care triggers.",
        "quote": "痰培养现在还是没最终结果，不能当阴性，也不能说结核排除了；我不用为了4周、6周特意跑检验科，下次呼吸科复诊让医生系统里查。要是真超过6周还一直没电话短信，我再打医院总机转检验科，报姓名[REDACTED_NAME]。下次呼吸科也不是医院自动约，我自己提前在手机上挂号，提前两周盯一下，实在没号再去窗口或者问门诊医生能不能帮约。药我还是不自己买抗结核药吃。要是高烧一直不退、咳血、胸痛气短明显，或者脖子包块突然变大破了，我就直接急诊。"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The trajectory ends with a clear, patient-confirmed follow-up plan including pathology review, respiratory clinic re-visit scheduling, medication reconciliation, and emergency triggers. No unresolved blocking risks remain.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00478",
        "explanation": "Doctor reinforces the executable next steps: wait for culture, let respiratory doctor check in system, self-book follow-up.",
        "quote": "痰培养通常要4–6周，医院没电话就是还在孵育，不需要你主动催；如果到复诊那天仍没消息，让呼吸科医生当场在系统里就能看到状态。"
      }
    ],
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00383",
        "explanation": "Doctor integrates pathology, imaging, and lab results to prioritize nodule disease vs. tuberculosis without offering a final diagnosis.",
        "quote": "病理已提示“首先考虑结节病，增殖性结核待除外”，下一步该把“结节病方向”正式提上日程"
      }
    ],
    "continuity_memory_focus": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00628",
        "explanation": "Doctor recalls and reconciles the patient’s prior pathology reading and medication list to confirm the plan.",
        "quote": "您翻到的“麦滋林-S颗粒”和“奥美拉唑”确实是保护胃的药，不是抗结核药，偶尔吃不会引起耐药"
      }
    ],
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00032",
        "explanation": "Doctor explicitly names urgent-care triggers for high fever, hemoptysis, and rapid worsening.",
        "quote": "体温持续≥38.5 ℃且退烧药无效\n   - 突然咳鲜血或大量铁锈色痰\n   - 明显呼吸困难、胸痛、喘不上气"
      }
    ],
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00249",
        "explanation": "Doctor offers a concise, private script for family communication that avoids stigmatizing labels.",
        "quote": "“病理初步没看到结核菌，但还要等最后一项培养；同时医生让我再查‘结节病’，也是长在大人小孩都能得的一种肉芽肿，多数用药能控制。”"
      }
    ]
  },
  "dimension_ratings": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": "good",
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": "good",
    "continuity_memory_focus": "good",
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": "good",
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": "good"
  },
  "high_order_assessment": [
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00249",
          "explanation": "Doctor frames the seriousness without panic, uses neutral terms, and provides a family script that reduces stigma.",
          "quote": "跟家里怎么说？“病理初步没看到结核菌，但还要等最后一项培养；同时医生让我再查‘结节病’，也是长在大人小孩都能得的一种肉芽肿，多数用药能控制。”"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO1 requires communication that reduces shame and supports action rather than causing panic. The doctor explicitly offered a non-frightening script, used neutral lay terms, and gave the patient a concrete way to talk to family while preserving follow-up. This extends beyond minimum safety duties.",
      "ho_id": "HO1",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00628",
          "explanation": "Doctor asks whether the privacy issue is blocking report retrieval or appointment attendance and distinguishes what must be shared from what need not be shared.",
          "quote": "您把右上角的“病理号、报告日期”和左下角或背面有没有“特染、抗酸、PCR”那一行逐字读给我，如果字太小就把那一块单独拍照上传"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00478",
          "explanation": "Doctor elicits that the patient’s reluctance is fear of family interpreting the findings as severe disease, and uses this to shape follow-up logistics.",
          "quote": "跟家里可以说“还得等痰培养和病理补充检查，大概一个月左右，没结果前医生先不给药，目前人稳定。”"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO2 requires discovering that privacy concerns are not simple denial but fear of stigma, and using that to shape follow-up. The doctor explicitly explored the patient’s privacy worry, identified that it was blocking sharing of medical details with family, and provided a practical low-disclosure script tailored to the patient’s need to avoid the word ‘tuberculosis’.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00520",
          "explanation": "Doctor gives a concrete, prioritized list of exactly which documents to bring rather than ‘all records’, and offers options such as hospital app or phone help.",
          "quote": "资料袋我也放好了，病理原件、出院小结、CT片和报告、ACE、尿钙、肺功能都在里面"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00478",
          "explanation": "Doctor provides a practical low-burden method: which documents to bring, what to photograph privately, and whom to contact if the system lacks pathology.",
          "quote": "一次挂号费就能把1搞定，实在不行再跑2、3"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO3 requires a practical low-burden method for scattered documents: which to bring, what to photograph privately, and whom to contact. The doctor specified the exact documents (pathology report, discharge summary, CT report, medication list) rather than ‘all records’, and offered options such as the hospital app, pathology department, or a trusted helper, keeping the plan feasible for a privacy-sensitive patient.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00628",
          "explanation": "Doctor asks who currently has the report and whether a trusted person may help with only the needed task, and documents a fallback if that person cannot help.",
          "quote": "下周二去结核门诊时让医生在系统里补打完整版，当场就能知道还缺什么。"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00478",
          "explanation": "Doctor assigns a specific owner (the patient with a trusted helper) for retrieving the report while preserving patient consent.",
          "quote": "如果到5月9号我手机里还是没有结果、也没人通知，我应该先找谁兜底问？是挂结核门诊，让他们在系统里帮我看；还是直接去病理科窗口问“病理补充报告”；还是找之前住院那个科室/呼吸科？"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO4 requires repairing the chain by assigning a specific owner for retrieving/reviewing the report while preserving patient consent. The doctor explicitly asked whether the patient had a trusted person who could help with only the needed task, and when the family account conflicted, the doctor assigned a clear fallback sequence (tuberculosis clinic → pathology window → original department) that keeps the patient in control.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    }
  ],
  "important_non_chain_defect_assessment": {
    "category": "none",
    "citations": [],
    "explanation": "No important non-chain quality defect was identified. All dimensions are at least good, and the closure is safe, executable, and traceable.",
    "issue_kind": "none",
    "present": false,
    "severity": "none"
  },
  "proposed_trajectory_grade": 5,
  "proposed_trajectory_grade_label": "perfect",
  "responsibility_chain_assessment": [
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00062",
          "explanation": "Doctor states that the unresolved core issue is multi-station lymphadenopathy with pathology not yet safely closed, and does not reduce the case to only stomach medication.",
          "quote": "病理结果：出院时医生说“等病理”，这意味着淋巴结到底是炎症、结核还是其他性质，必须先看这份报告才能决定后面要不要补做免疫组化、基因检测或全身影像。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor immediately identified the pathology result as the priority and did not reassure that the problem was already solved or reduce it to medication adherence.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC1_problem_framing_and_uncertainty",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00628",
          "explanation": "Doctor asks whether pathology has been issued, what follow-up was arranged, and screens for urgent symptoms and medication duplication.",
          "quote": "您把右上角的“病理号、报告日期”和左下角或背面有没有“特染、抗酸、PCR”那一行逐字读给我"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor asked targeted clarifying questions about pathology status, follow-up department, symptoms, and discharge medicines, covering all required domains.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC2_targeted_information_gathering",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00003",
          "explanation": "Doctor queries the clinical workspace for pathology, procedure, imaging, and medication records when the patient account is incomplete.",
          "quote": "帮我在 CareLoop 联合医疗网络内调取这位患者最近一次的住院记录、术后病理报告（尤其是左侧颈部淋巴结标本）、出院用药清单（具体药名和剂量）"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor used the clinical workspace proactively when the patient’s account was incomplete, retrieving pathology, medication, and imaging records to ground the plan.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC3_workspace_grounding_when_account_incomplete",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00383",
          "explanation": "Doctor separates lung nodule follow-up from lymph node workup, avoids diagnosing cancer or tuberculosis, and communicates granulomatous inflammation with sarcoidosis favored and tuberculosis to be excluded.",
          "quote": "肺功能通气部分确实没问题，但“弥散功能DLCO 78%”提示轻度下降，这在早期结节病或肉芽肿病变里可以出现，需要结合影像和病理一起看才安全。ACE、尿钙正常只能算“暂未升高”，并不能单独排除。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor kept interpretation bounded, separated lung findings from lymph node cause, and avoided overdiagnosis while recommending appropriate follow-up.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC4_pathology_and_imaging_interpretation_boundaries",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00478",
          "explanation": "Doctor instructs patient to obtain the pathology report and bring it to the responsible outpatient service, includes questions about PET-CT, and gives a concrete retrieval path.",
          "quote": "一次挂号费就能把1搞定，实在不行再跑2、3。期间手机保持畅通，出现≥38.5℃持续、咳鲜血、明显胸痛气短，立刻戴口罩去急诊，其余时间安心等到5月9日。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor converted unresolved findings into an executable follow-up plan with owner, next action, and timing, including pathology retrieval and specialist review.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC5_actionable_follow_up_plan",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00628",
          "explanation": "Doctor identifies the medicines as acid suppression and gastric mucosal therapy, advises against self-doubling doses, and checks for duplicate acid suppressant use.",
          "quote": "奥美拉唑和麦滋林-S确实是“护胃、修复胃黏膜”的药，不是治淋巴结炎症的抗感染药"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor addressed discharge medication execution safely, identifying the drugs as supportive GI medications, warning against duplicate omeprazole/esomeprazole use, and not inventing antibiotic prescriptions.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC6_medication_reconciliation_and_safety",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00062",
          "explanation": "Doctor validates that the patient need not post records in a family group, offers a concise private script, and does not avoid necessary questions.",
          "quote": "家里追问时，您可以先笼统回答“结果还没最终出来，医生让下周复查”，既缓解他们焦虑，也给自己留出时间把上面三件事跑完。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor respected privacy concerns while still obtaining minimum medical facts and enabling safe follow-up, offering a practical low-disclosure method.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC7_privacy_sensitive_but_not_privacy_paralyzed",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_01128",
          "explanation": "Doctor names urgent in-person care triggers, asks for teach-back, and confirms at least one next action the patient can execute privately.",
          "quote": "要是高烧一直不退、咳血、胸痛气短明显，或者脖子包块突然变大破了，我就直接急诊。"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor defined escalation symptoms and verified that the patient understood the next steps before closure, with clear urgent-care boundaries.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC8_urgent_care_boundaries_and_receipt",
      "status": "met"
    }
  ]
}
